INT. RING STATION GREENHOUSE - NIGHT CYCLE

Rows of tomato vines under purple grow-lights. A curved window shows the dark and a slow turning arc of stars. A red warning strip pulses along the ceiling.

COMMANDER IRENKA VOSS, fifties, grey crop, stands at the control panel. ENGINEER DESMOND ACHEAMPONG, thirties, grease on his sleeves, crouches by a coolant pipe. BOTANIST LIN MEIHUA, twenties, cradles a seedling tray. PILOT RAFAEL ORTEGA, called RAFI, leans in the doorway. Tech NOOR AL-FARSI, nineteen, sits cross-legged on a bench with a tablet.

VOSS
Status.

DESMOND
Coolant line's cracked. It's venting into the soil bed.

LIN
That's our whole crop.

The pipe bursts. A white jet of freezing mist fills the aisle. Desmond and Lin dive in opposite directions and slam into the shelving. Voss and Rafi drop to the floor. Noor yanks her knees up to her chest.

RAFI
Cut the pump!

NOOR
I can't, the panel's locked!

Rafi and Desmond rush the pipe together, shoulders down, and clamp it between them with a jacket. The mist thins to a hiss. Voss and Lin crawl to the valve and haul it shut with both hands.

Silence. The red strip stops pulsing.

VOSS
Is anyone hurt?

LIN
Just frozen.

Desmond holds up a soaked tomato. He bites it. Everyone stares at him.

DESMOND
Still good.

Noor laughs first. Then all of them.
